*** Add File:ops/carbon/README_INTEGRATION.md
+Integration & quickstart
+
+1) Prometheus exporter:
+   - Deploy ops/carbon/deployment/carbon-exporter-deployment.yaml to your cluster (or run exporter locally).
+   - Ensure Prometheus scrapes exporter on configured port (default 9810).
+
+2) WattTime API:
+   - Set WATTTIME_API_KEY env var for exporter or local fetch scripts.
+   - If unavailable, exporter can fall back to cloud provider estimated intensities or static values.
+
+3) Per-job emissions:
+   - Invoke ops/carbon/job_emissions.py from training/inference wrappers to estimate and log energy & CO2e to MLflow.
+   - Example: python3 ops/carbon/job_emissions.py --run-id <mlflow_run_id> --duration-sec 3600 --avg-power-w 250
+
+4) Carbon-aware scheduler:
+   - Run carbon_scheduler.py on a control host or as a pod (with RBAC & kubeconfig).
+   - Submit job manifests with ops/carbon/cli_submit.py which places manifests into scheduler queue.
+   - Scheduler will wait for intensity below threshold before kubectl apply.
+
+5) Dashboards & reporting:
+   - Import ops/carbon/grafana/carbon_dashboard.json to Grafana.
+   - Schedule .github/workflows/carbon_report.yml or run locally to aggregate and store carbon reports in MLflow.
+
